          "category": "code_insight",
          "analysis": "The binary is a DDoS (Distributed Denial of Service) bot for ARM Linux systems, likely targeting IoT devices. Upon execution, it daemonizes itself by forking twice and calling `setsid`. It then connects to a hardcoded C2 server, announces its presence, and waits for commands. The malware is capable of launching multiple types of network floods, indicated by command-parsing logic for attacks like `TCP`, `UDP`, `VSE`, `STOMP`, and `STDHEX`. The `vseattack` function specifically crafts packets for a Valve Source Engine query flood. A highly indicative IOC is the taunting string \"dayzddos.co runs you if you read this lol...\", confirming its malicious purpose as a DDoS tool.",
          "source": "palm",
          "verdict": "malicious",
          "id": "a50504c871c093d1124eb59c695a9b9b9a95db2b115b39f47f72b015baa896b5-file-palm"
